deployment-start = Start installation backup
deployment-revoke = Review runner revocation
deployment-revoke-impact = Revocation cancels queued tasks and rejects further exchanges. An already running operation still needs local reconciliation and may no longer report its result.
deployment-cancel-impact = Cancel this queued operation. A started task cannot be cancelled and requires its local recovery workflow.
deployment-confirm-action = Confirm operation
deployment-back = Back
deployment-task = Deployment task
deployment-succeeded = Runner reports backup encrypted and original services healthy. Isolated restore verification is a separate task.
deployment-recovery = Local recovery required. Check the durable task journal on the deployment host.
deployment-cancelled = Cancelled before execution
deployment-waiting = Waiting for execution or a confirmed runner result; missing observations remain unknown.
deployment-unknown = Unknown
deployment-cancel = Review task cancellation
deployment-more = Load more deployment tasks

capacity-title = Relay capacity and observation
capacity-boundary = Samples actual framed bytes every 10 seconds across Peer and backbone carriers; excludes IP, TCP, TLS and QUIC overhead. Accepted writes are neither billed traffic nor end-to-end delivery.
capacity-select = Select capacity host
capacity-refresh = Refresh capacity
capacity-fresh = Current observation · resource accessibility is checked separately
capacity-unknown = Unknown or stale · check the Relay management connection and refresh
capacity-observed = Last Control receipt
capacity-sessions = Admitted Peer sessions (primary and standby)
capacity-read = Framed bytes read in this process
capacity-write = Framed bytes accepted in this process
capacity-queue = Messages waiting in Peer queues
capacity-queue-bytes = Encoded bytes waiting in Peer queues
capacity-backbone = Occupied backbone queue slots
capacity-audit = Occupied audit queue slots
capacity-backpressure = Queue rejections increased between samples: check uplink capacity, slow clients and queue limits.
capacity-audit-dropped = Audit drops increased between samples: check database health and audit write load; records may be incomplete.
capacity-invalid = Invalid forwarded frames increased: check Relay versions and error logs.

operations-status-title = Operations status and pending issues
operations-status-refresh = Refresh operations status
operations-audit-boundary = Audit storage includes tables, indexes and TOAST. Row counts and growth are PostgreSQL estimates; resets or missing baselines make growth unknown. These statistics do not prove audit completeness.
operations-audit-bytes = Audit storage bytes
operations-audit-rows = Estimated audit rows
operations-audit-growth = Estimated inserted rows per hour
operations-backup-unknown = No successful backup has been reported. Review or create an installation backup task.
operations-backup-reported = A runner reported a successful backup; restore verification and activation require separate checks.
operations-no-alerts = Current samples show no monitored operations issue. Use resource diagnostics to verify application access.
operations-audit-unknown = Audit capacity is unknown: check the database connection and refresh.
operations-relay-unknown = Some Relays have no current sample: review capacity observations and host management connections.
operations-relay-failed = A Relay maintenance task failed: review its cause and readiness before retrying.
operations-recovery-required = Installation recovery is incomplete: run the restricted recovery command on that installation and check the original services.
operations-backup-failed = The latest backup failed: review its cause, refresh the preview and create a new task.
operations-status-unknown = Operations status is unknown. Refresh or check the Control service.
operations-next-actions = Operations checks

deployment-upgrade-impact = This role will restart using the staged signed release. Existing connections may reconnect; database changes are not rolled back.

deployment-upgrade-repair = This explicitly repairs a failed native transaction with a newer signed release.

deployment-upgrade-start = Start staged upgrade

deployment-upgrade-task = Native role upgrade

deployment-backup-task = Installation backup

deployment-upgrade-succeeded = Upgrade completed; the runner checked the selected executable and readiness.

deployment-recover = Review native recovery
deployment-superseded = A newer signed repair replaced this failed upgrade. Check the replacement task for its outcome.

deployment-recover-impact = After fixing the local cause, resume this exact role transaction. This may restart the role. It does not roll back Control data or choose a different release.

policy-priority-help = Lower priorities match first; ties prefer deny, then rule ID. Changing priority affects access. Validate and simulate before publishing.

relay-region = Relay region (lowercase letters, digits or hyphens)
relay-routing-weight = Routing weight (1–1000)
invalid-policy-draft = The rule draft is invalid or its priority limit has been reached. Review the advanced editor; existing rules are retained.
invalid-policy-devices = Choose two different valid devices.
